# The site is generated, and the generators write LF. Every blob in here is
# already LF, and the live server sends LF.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites all 2,549 pages to CRLF when
# somebody clones fresh. The next build writes them back as LF, so git
# reports the entire site as modified and a real change becomes impossible
# to see. Found by restoring from the build branch into a clean directory
# and rebuilding: content was identical, and git still showed 2,553 files
# changed.
#
# -text means store and check out these bytes unaltered, which is what a
# generated site wants.
* -text
